! mcp_bootstrap_p112.strap -- printed page 112, the tail of the
! SERIAL interrupt table and the head of the PARALLEL interrupt
! table.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.119, header READ AND NOT
! ASSUMED: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID DB000068  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 112", and the
! column-head line's own right-hand "LOCATION" field prints 215100,
! which is this page's first location.
!
! FIFTY-ONE LINES, COUNTED NOT ESTIMATED.  The printed LINE column
! runs 1..51 with no gap and the page is blank below line 51.  The
! card-serial column runs DB000068 (line 1) through DB000098 (line
! 51).  THE WHOLE COLUMN WAS RENDERED AND READ, in three overlapping
! crops at 600 dpi (lines 1-22, 23-43, 42-51); the last four serials
! are DB000097, DB000097, DB000098, DB000098 and below line 51 the
! form is blank.  That is THIRTY-ONE CARDS for fifty-one lines,
! because a SIC and the
! branch that completes its 64-bit instruction are punched on ONE
! card and listed on TWO lines with the SAME serial (lines 1+2 are
! both DB000068, 9+10 are both DB000073, and so on).  The serial
! prefix is "DB": printed p.104's prefix was read "CB" and NOT
! claimed with confidence, and at 600 dpi on this page the glyph has
! the straight vertical left stem of a D in every one of the thirty-
! one serials.  (The header's own CARD ID repeats line 1's serial.)
!
! >>> WHAT THE PAGE IS. <<<  Three more entries of the serial
! interrupt table (lines 1-6), then S IPT, the base of the PARALLEL
! interrupt table (line 7), then the parallel table's own entries.
! Each table slot is one 64-bit "SIC,<save area> / B,<routine>" pair:
! the SIC stores the instruction counter into the save area and the
! branch enters the routine.  Three kinds of slot appear:
!   lines 1-6   SIC,ST IO   / BD,S IPT+45..47.   -- serial table
!   lines 9-10  SIC,S INTO  / B,JWLODE           -- the TS slot
!   lines 18+   SIC,W INTOR / B,W LODE           -- every other slot
! and lines 12-16 are five BRANCH ON ZERO BIT instructions, one per
! parallel I-O interrupt class, each testing a bit of S PS IOI and
! branching to K STORE.
!
! >>> THE PAGE'S OWN STRUCTURE IS CORROBORATED BY A PRIMARY SOURCE.
! docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt, the interrupt
! table, prints two rows that are exactly lines 8-10 and lines 17-19
! of this page:
!     "MASKABLE TS ... STIC SIPT+4.0   SINTO    JW LODE"
!     "All other  ... STIC SIPT+       WINTOR   WLODE"
! and its I-O row names "SPSIOI (receptor)" and "KSTORE" -- "The
! receptor is entered at KSTORE from the parallel ... interrupt
! table with a bit set in SPSIOI corresponding ...".  That settles
! by document every glyph on this page that shape alone cannot:
! S INTO (not SINTC), W INTOR (not WINTCR), W LODE and JWLODE (not
! WLCDE/JWLCDE), S PS IOI (not SPSICI) and K STORE.  Every one of
! those six names has an O in the position this drum prints open.
!
! >>> ONE REAL SURPRISE, AND IT IS NOT A MISREADING. <<<  Line 9's
! "SIC,S INTO" and line 18's "SIC,W INTOR" compile the SAME binary,
! "216371.40 80".  Both were re-read at 900 dpi: the statements are
! six characters apart (S-I-N-T-O against W-I-N-T-O-R) and cannot be
! confused, and both binary fields read 216371.40.  So S INTO and
! W INTOR are two names for ONE half-word save area at 216371.40 --
! which is what the Analysis Guide's table implies when it lists them
! in the same column.  They are SYN'd to the same value below and the
! fact is recorded rather than "fixed".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE PAGE SITS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The ORIGIN IS NOT SET BY A CARD ON THIS PAGE -- there is no SLC
! before line 1.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! counter to 0o215000 and printed p.111's last line (line 50) is a
! BD at 215077.40, a half word that ends exactly at 215100.00, where
! this page's line 1 begins.  THE JOIN IS CONTIGUOUS.  This deck
! writes the arriving counter as a hard "SLC, (8)215100." so that it
! assembles standalone; when pp.105-111 land, that SLC is the row to
! reconsider (see printed p.104's note on the same point).
!
! THE PAGE LEAVES THE COUNTER AT 215147.00 -- line 51's half-word
! branch at 215146.40 ends there -- and the OCR of PDF p.120
! (printed p.113) prints its line 1 as "215147.00  216371.40 80
! SIC,WINTOR".  BOTH JOINS ARE CONTIGUOUS, backward and forward.
!
! pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block that printed p.2 opened
! and printed p.98 line 37 closed with "UNTAIL,(2)", so names here
! may legitimately repeat names defined in pp.2-98 at different
! addresses.  None of this page's eight names collides with one in
! the transcribed decks.
!
! THE LOCATION COUNTER JUMPS FIVE TIMES, each time by an SLC that
! names a slot of the parallel table (lines 8, 11, 17, 20, 23).  The
! words skipped are 215104-215106, 215110-215113, 215121-215124,
! 215126 and 215130: slots of the table that other pages fill.  From
! line 24 (215131.00) to line 51 (215146.40) the page is contiguous.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE of the fifty-one line numbers carries an asterisk right
! after it ("7*", "51*").  That is the ordinary column and is not a
! mark.
!
! SIX lines carry a SECOND asterisk after the LOCATION, the
! unexplained marker of docs/listing_typography.md 12: lines 8, 11,
! 17, 20, 23 and 46.  Five of the six are exactly this page's five
! SLC rows, which is suggestive and which I CHECKED AND THEN HAD TO
! DROP.  The tempting reading -- "an SLC row carries the mark" --
! predicts that every SLC row in every transcribed deck carries it,
! and TWO ROWS SAY OTHERWISE:
!     printed p.99  line 11  215000.00    SLC,(8)215000.   no mark
!     printed p.109 line  5  215020.71    SLC,$            no mark
! and the second is decisive, because printed p.104 line 6 is the
! SAME STATEMENT AT THE SAME LOCATION -- "215020.71 * SLC,$" -- and
! IS marked.  One statement, one location, two pages, mark on one
! only.  So the correlation on this page is a coincidence of this
! page, and the equivalent "gap marker" reading (the five SLC rows
! are exactly the five rows where the counter jumps) dies with it,
! as it already died on printed p.3.
!
! LINE 46 IS THE SIXTH AND FITS NEITHER: an ordinary "SIC,W INTOR"
! at 215144.00 WITH binary beside the asterisk ("216371.40 80", read
! at 900 dpi), preceded by a half-word branch at 215143.40 that ends
! exactly at 215144.00, so no gap and no SLC.  Recorded as open, per
! docs/listing_typography.md 12, with nothing added to it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! HOW THE BINARY WAS SETTLED, FIELD BY FIELD
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every byte on this page sits in one of five shapes, and each one
! was settled on WHAT PRODUCED IT, not on ink:
!
! * "215265.00 80" (SIC).  Per listing_oracle's format note, bits
!   0-17 print as the octal word, bits 18-23 as two octal digits and
!   bits 24-31 as two hex.  SIC shares the literal 1000 at bits
!   24-27 with BRANCH ON BIT (strap/opcodes.py, X22-6533), and its
!   index field is empty here, so the byte is 80 and cannot be B0:
!   B0 would need bits 28-31 = 0000 with bit 24-27 = 1011, which is
!   not SIC's literal.
! * "215160.04 00" / "216604.50 00" / "215103.20 00" (half-word
!   branches).  The top bit of the octal pair is bit 18, the branch
!   target's HALF-WORD SELECT; bits 19-23 are the branch modifier.
!   The three modifiers on this page are therefore BD = 00100,
!   B = 01000 and BEW = 10000, and they are CONSISTENT ACROSS THE
!   PAGE: every one of the twenty-eight "B,W LODE" rows prints .10
!   (b18=0, 01000) and every one of the three "BD,S IPT+n." rows
!   prints .04 (b18=0, 00100).  JWLODE's .50 is 101000 -- b18=1,
!   so its target is 216604.40, a SECOND half word, and the modifier
!   is B's own 01000.  The hex byte of every branch is 00.
! * "215226.11 80  215710.34 0C" (BRANCH ON ZERO BIT AND SET TO ONE).
!   Checked field by field against strap/opcodes.py BB_CODES, whose
!   source is X22-6533 "BRANCH ON BIT -- Strap Format: OP,B,(I),A(K)":
!   first half = the 24-bit BIT address (word 215226, bit 0o11 = 9
!   decimal = the ".9" in the statement) with the 1000 literal and a
!   zero index, giving 80; second half = the 19-bit branch address in
!   bits 32-50 (215710, half-word select 0, the top bit of 0o34),
!   then the literal 111000000 at 51-59 (0o34's low five bits 11100
!   plus 0x0C's top four 0000), then mod = 11 and cond = 0 at bits
!   60-62 and K = 0 at bit 63 -- which is BZB1 and nothing else.
!   THE LOW NIBBLE C IS THE MODIFIER, NOT AN INDEX, and the five
!   rows' bit offsets .11 .12 .13 .14 .15 are 9 10 11 12 13 decimal,
!   exactly the statements' +.9 +.10 +.11 +.12 +.13.
! * The round glyphs.  This page prints 0 open constantly ("2151CC"
!   for 215100 in the OCR of its own location column), and the octal
!   fields -- which cannot hold a C -- are the calibration: line 1's
!   location prints 215100.00 with both zeros open at 400 dpi and
!   closed at 900.  Every "C" in a binary field on this page is in a
!   position that is either octal (so a 0 with certainty) or part of
!   a hex byte whose value the paragraph above derives from the
!   statement.  NO byte here was settled by ink alone.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE STATEMENT COLUMN PRINTS vs WHAT THIS DECK WRITES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! MCP's names carry blanks ("S IPT", "W LODE", "S PS IOI") and the
! listing prints them as punched, INCONSISTENTLY: line 2 prints
! "BD,SIPT+45." and line 11 prints "SLC,S IPT+9.0" for the same
! symbol.  As in every deck here, the blanks are dropped and the
! name is written solid.  The printed form is kept in the listing
! block below, verbatim.
!
! >>> FIVE OF THE SEVEN EXTERNALS ARE CORROBORATED AT THEIR OWN
! DEFINING CARDS, on pages this project has NOT yet transcribed.
! docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt is a full-volume OCR of the same
! PDF; it is garbled and is a CROSS-CHECK, NOT A SOURCE, but it is
! legible enough to name a symbol and its location:
!   printed p.116 line  1  215226.00  S PS IOI  XW,0
!                                     "-I/O INTERRUPT PRESERVATION WORD"
!   printed p.116 line  9  215265.00  S T IO    VF,0
!   printed p.130 line ~8  216333.00  W LODE    T,0,3-...
!   printed p.130 line 50  216371.40  W INTOR   VF,0
!                                     "- INTERRUPT PRESERVATION WORD"
!   printed p.130 line 51  216371.40+           S INTO  SYN,W INTOR
!   printed p.134 line 38  216604.40  JWLODE    T16,3-...
! >>> THE LAST OF THOSE SETTLES THE SURPRISE ABOVE OUTRIGHT. <<<
! S INTO is not a coincidence and not a misreading: printed p.130
! defines it with a SYN card whose operand IS W INTOR, which is why
! the two compile the same half-word address here.  The reading
! "S INTO and W INTOR are two names for one save area" was arrived
! at from this page's binary alone and is then confirmed by the card
! that does it.
!
! K STORE is the ONE external with no second witness: the OCR's only
! legible occurrences of 215710 are this page's own five rows.  Its
! NAME is corroborated by the Analysis Guide prose quoted above; its
! ADDRESS rests on this page's binary, which is stated here because
! the !CHECK rows that use it cannot test it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- every address below is READ OFF THIS PAGE'S OWN
! BINARY OUTPUT COLUMN, and a !CHECK on such a row therefore tests
! the opcode and modifier bits, not the address (listing_oracle's
! docstring says so).  S IPT is the one symbol this page DEFINES,
! and the three "BD,S IPT+45..47." rows ARE a real address check,
! because their targets are computed from it.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)215100.
! The last glyph of this name is a C, not an O.  This deck first
! read it as STIO; at 1200 dpi it is open on the right and the SAME
! SHAPE as the C of "SIC" at the start of its own row, and printed
! pp.110 and 111 spell it STIC at this same 215265.00.  Caught by
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py.
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! line  1 "SIC,ST IO"
SINTO   SYN, (8)216371.40            ! line  9 "SIC,S INTO"
JWLODE  SYN, (8)216604.40            ! line 10 "B,JWLODE" prints 216604.50
SPSIOI  SYN, (8)215226.0             ! line 12 "BZB1,S PS IOI+.9 ,..."
KSTORE  SYN, (8)215710.0             ! line 12 ",K STORE"
WINTOR  SYN, (8)216371.40            ! line 18 "SIC,W INTOR" -- SAME AS S INTO
WLODE   SYN, (8)216333.0             ! line 19 "B,W LODE"

        SLC, (8)215100.
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  1
        BD, SIPT+45.                 ! line  2
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  3
        BD, SIPT+46.                 ! line  4
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  5
        BD, SIPT+47.                 ! line  6
SIPT    BEW, $                       ! line  7 -BASE ADDRESS OF PARALLEL
!                                              INTERRUPT T  <- the comment
!                                              ENDS at that bare "T", with
!                                              clear paper between it and
!                                              the card-serial column: the
!                                              card's own comment field ran
!                                              out mid-word.  "T(ABLE)" is
!                                              NOT transcribed, only noted.
        SLC, SIPT+4.0                ! line  8
        SIC, SINTO                   ! line  9
        B, JWLODE                    ! line 10 -SPECIAL ROUTINE FOR TS
        SLC, SIPT+9.0                ! line 11 -PARALLEL IO INTERRUPT SLOTS
        BZB1, SPSIOI+.9,KSTORE       ! line 12 -EPGK PARALLEL INTERRUPT
        BZB1, SPSIOI+.10,KSTORE      ! line 13 -UK PARALLEL INTERRUPT
        BZB1, SPSIOI+.11,KSTORE      ! line 14 -EE PARALLEL INTERRUPT
        BZB1, SPSIOI+.12,KSTORE      ! line 15 -EOP PARALLEL INTERRUPT
        BZB1, SPSIOI+.13,KSTORE      ! line 16 - CS PARALLEL INTERRUPT
        SLC, SIPT+18.0               ! line 17
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 18
        B, WLODE                     ! line 19
        SLC, SIPT+20.0               ! line 20
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 21
        B, WLODE                     ! line 22
        SLC, SIPT+22.0               ! line 23
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 24
        B, WLODE                     ! line 25
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 26
        B, WLODE                     ! line 27
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 28
        B, WLODE                     ! line 29
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 30
        B, WLODE                     ! line 31
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 32
        B, WLODE                     ! line 33
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 34
        B, WLODE                     ! line 35
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 36
        B, WLODE                     ! line 37
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 38
        B, WLODE                     ! line 39
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 40
        B, WLODE                     ! line 41
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 42
        B, WLODE                     ! line 43
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 44
        B, WLODE                     ! line 45
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 46
        B, WLODE                     ! line 47
        SIC, WINTOR                  ! line 48
        B, WLODE                     ! line 49
